k summary:\n\n- **Energy Savings from LED Upgrade**: You’ll save 450 kWh per day (164,250 kWh annually), reducing carbon emissions by ~118.5 tons per year.\n- **Current Power Status**: Your main office is running at 67% load on 120V — stable but nearing capacity.\n- **Solar Generation Potential**: At 40.7128° N, 74.0060° W, with 250 m² of monocrystalline panels at 15% efficiency, you can generate approximately 112.5 kWh per day (41,062.5 kWh/year).\n- **Substation Update**: Successfully adjusted from 120V to 220V as requested.\n\nYes, the solar estimate is precisely for the coordinates you provided: 40.7128° N, 74.0060° W. All calculations are location- and panel-specific.\nuser: I need to send out a customer satisfaction survey to all our customers via email. Can you handle that?\nassistant: I\'d be happy to help you send out a customer satisfaction survey! To proceed, I need a few details:\n\n1. What questions would you like included in the survey? (e.g., rating scale, open-ended feedback, etc.)\n2. Who should be listed as the sender? (e.g., \'Customer Success Team\' or your name)\n3. Would you like to set a deadline for responses? (optional but recommended)\n\nCould you provide the survey questions and sender name first?\nuser: Sure! The survey should ask: \'How satisfied are you with our service? (1-5)\', \'What did we do well?\', and \'How can we improve?\'. Send it from \'Customer Success Team\', and let’s set the deadline for next Friday.\nassistant: Thanks for the details! I’ll now send the survey to all customers with your specified questions, sender, and deadline.\nassistant: Great! The customer satisfaction survey has been successfully sent to all 1,247 customers. The survey was sent from \'Customer Success Team\' with the deadline set for next Friday. You can track responses using survey ID: srv_789xyz. Let me know if you’d like a summary report once responses start coming in!<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_pena