e are afraid that they will gain weight when they quit smoking, so they may feel insecure and inactive.\nuser: By the way, why do people suddenly gain weight after quitting smoking?\nassistant: There are several reasons. Some of them:\nSmoking can suppress appetite, so a person who smokes does not feel intense hunger.\nSmoking increases metabolism, so a person who smokes burns calories faster.\nFinally, some people may choose to replace smoking with food, which may also contribute to weight gain.\n\nBut giving up another cigarette does not mean that you will definitely gain extra pounds. There are a large number of reviews from those who have already quit the addiction without gaining a single gram of excess fat.\nAnd it\'s important to note that the health benefits of quitting far outweigh the potential for weight gain.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=2000, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: None, lora_request: None, prompt_adapter_request: None.
