INFO 09-21 18:28:11 logger.py:37] Received request chatcmpl-31fff612ccd44178afc94628c2dedfa9: prompt: '<|im_start|>system\nYou are building a long-term memory for an AI assistant. From the dialogue excerpt, extract atomic fact memories as a JSON object: {"memories": ["<single declarative sentence>", ...]}. Keep identifiers, addresses, URLs and configuration values VERBATIM. One fact per entry; include the user preference, attribute or event each entry refers to. Output JSON only.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nDialogue excerpt:\nassistant: The question of who discovered America is complex, and there are several possible answers depending on how you define "discover" and "America." But in general terms, the discovery of America is usually attributed to Christopher Columbus, who in 1492 led the expedition that reached the Bahamas believing that he had reached the Indies.\n\nHowever, the claim that it was not actually Columbus who discovered America is a claim that has been made in recent times for various historical and cultural reasons. Here we present some of them:\n\n1. The previous existence of indigenous populations: America was not an "unknown" continent before the arrival of Columbus. There were indigenous populations that already inhabited these lands and had their own cultures and civilizations. Therefore, the claim that Columbus "discovered" America implies ignoring the previous existence of these populations.\n2. Other previous expeditions: There are historical records of other expeditions that reached America before Columbus\'s expedition, such as the Viking expedition led by Leif Erikson in the 11th century. Therefore, the claim that Columbus "discovered" America implies ignoring the existence of these previous expeditions.\n3. Error in the belief of having reached the Indies: Although Columbus arrived in America, he believed that he had arrived in the Indies, so he called the natives he found there "Indians." This mistaken belief has led some to question whether Columbus really discovered America or simply arrived at a place he thought was something it wasn\'t.\n\nIn short, the claim that Christopher Columbus did not discover America is a claim that has been made to point out that the idea of \u200b\u200ba "discovery" implies ignoring the previous existence of indigenous populations and the presence of other previous expeditions. The term "discovery" is also questioned due to the mistake Columbus made when he believed he had reached the Indies.\nuser: God exists?\nassistant: From a purely philosophical and scientific perspective, there is no indisputable evidence that may prove God\'s existence. The existence of God is a matter of faith and is the subject of philosophers, theologians and scientists discussed for centuries.\n\nThere are many religions and traditions that teach the existence of a supreme creature or some of the highest creatures, but these beliefs are based on spiritual revelations or experiences in empirical evidence. Therefore, the existence of God can be practiced from different perspectives and can be understood in different ways, according to individual religions, cultures and beliefs of each person.\n\nIn short, the existence of God has been debatment for centuries and will probably be the case in the future.\nuser: Write a text, with spelling mistakes so that I can write it correctly as a dictation, then correct my version and list the mistakes if there are any.\nassistant: Here is the text with spelling mistakes:\n"Once upon a time there was a man who had beautiful houses in the city and in the countryside, gold and silver dishes, furniture covered in the finest brocade and carriages all gilded. But unfortunately, this man had a blue beard; this gave him such an ugly and terrible appearance that all the women and girls fled from him.\nOne of his bees, a distinguished lady, had two very beautiful legs. He asked for the hand of one of them, leaving it up to him to choose which one he would like to give her. Neither of them wanted it and they passed it on to each other, because they could not resign themselves to having a husband with a blue beard. But what upset them most was that he had already been married several times and no one knew what had happened to those women.\nTo get to know them, Blue Beard took them with his mother and three or four of his best friends, and some young people from the region, to one of his country houses, where they stayed eight full days. Their time was spent on walks, hunts, fishing, dances, feasts, snacks and dinners; No one slept and they spent the night between vromas and entertainment. In short, everything went so well that the youngest of the young women began to find that the owner of the house no longer had such a blue beard and that he was a very proper man."\nI don\'t have the ability to convert your voice to text yet, but if you type your version of the text, I can correct it for you and list any mistakes I find.\nuser: I\'m preparing a report on the political landscape and government structure in Canada for 2020. Firstly, I need to know the election results. Based on that, I\'d like a comparative analysis of healthcare policies between Canada and the US from 2015 to 2020. Finally, I\'d like a detailed analysis of Canada\'s government structure in 2020.\nassistant: I\'ll start by retrieving the 2020 Canadian federal election results for you.\nassistant: Thank you for the election data. Now I\'ll compare healthcare policies between Canada and the United States from 2015 to 2020.\nassistant: I\'ve analyzed the healthcare policy trends. Now I\'ll examine Canada\'s government structure in 2020 to complete your report.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=2000, mi