n what year was the game \'Fortnite: Battle Royale\' first released? - 2017\n6. Which video game features the character Ezio Auditore? - Assassin\'s Creed\n7. Which video game was the first to feature a playable character who can jump? - Donkey Kong\n8. What was the first video game that allowed players to save their progress? - The Legend of Zelda\n9. What is the best-selling video game of all time? - Minecraft\n10. Which video game character is often saving Princess Peach? - Mario\n11. What year was the game \'League of Legends\' released? - 2009\n12. What is the maximum number of players in a Fortnite Game? - 100\n13. Which game is considered the first \'first-person shooter\'? - Wolfenstein 3D\n14. In what year was the game \'PlayerUnknown\'s Battlegrounds\' released? - 2017\n15. What city is the setting for the game \'Fallout 4\'? - Boston\n16. What is the name of the Final Fantasy VII character who wields a ginormous sword? - Cloud Strife\n17. What is the full name of the protagonist in \'Assassin\'s Creed II\'? - Ezio Auditore da Firenze\n18. Which English actor plays the character of Alex \'Echo\' Moreau in \'Rainbow Six: Siege\'? - Katie Lyons\n19. What year was \'Overwatch\' released? - 2016\n20. What is the protagonist\'s default name in \'Fallout 4\'? - Sole Survivor\n\nTest your knowledge and see how many you can get right!\nuser: Task Sequence Steps and Actions\nSteps are the basic components of a task sequence. These may include commands such as:\nSetting up and recording the OS of a reference computer\nInstalling Windows, hardware drivers, Configuration Manager client, and software on the target computer\nStep actions define task sequence step commands. There are two types of actions:\nAn action defined using a command line string is called a custom action.\nAn action that is predefined by Configuration Manager is called a built-in action.\nassistant: Unfortunately, I am unable to extract either a question or a task from your request. Could you please rephrase it or clarify what I need to do?\nuser: Windows installation sequence:\n1. Prepare a media with a recorded Windows image of the desired version and insert it into the USB connector.\n2. Restart the computer and enter the BIOS when the computer is turned on.\n3. In the BIOS settings, specify the prepared media as the first boot device.\n4. Save the settings and restart your computer.\n5. Follow the Windows installation prompts and instructions.\n6. Upon completion of Windows installation, remove the prepared media from the USB; from this stage you no longer need it.\n7. After a forced reboot, follow the system instructions for setting up Windows.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=2000, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: None, lora_request: None, prompt_adapter_request: None.
