include action and dialog to bring the story to life and show the dynamics between the three characters. Let me know if you would like me to elaborate on the story further.\nuser: That is great. I want you to continue the story with Wonder Woman coming on batman\'s plane. And to the surprise of everyone she took the side of Cheshire, lassoing green arrow and yelling at him. "Do you feel lucky, punk?" she yelled. \nYou continue from here\nassistant: Green Arrow was stunned. He had always known Wonder Woman to be a champion of justice, and now she was taking the side of Cheshire?\n\n"What\'s going on here?" Green Arrow demanded as he struggled against the lasso.\n\n"Wonder Woman is right," Cheshire said with a smirk. "You and your buddy here have been interfering with my plans for too long. It\'s time we settled things once and for all."\n\nRed Arrow stepped forward, his bow at the ready. "We\'ll never let you get away with your crimes, Cheshire. You know that."\n\nCheshire laughed. "Oh, I know. But at least now I have the backing of a true Amazon warrior. And that means you\'re both as good as done for."\n\nGreen Arrow scowled. "We\'ll see about that."\n\nThe three archers clashed once more, arrows flying back and forth in a blur of motion. But this time, Cheshire had a new advantage with Wonder Woman by her side. The two women worked together in perfect harmony, their attacks relentless and precise.\n\nGreen Arrow and Red Arrow struggled to keep up, dodging and weaving as they tried to land their own shots. But it seemed like every time they got close, Wonder Woman or Cheshire would deflect their arrows with ease.\n\n"This is madness!" Green Arrow shouted as he stumbled back. "We can\'t keep this up forever!"\n\n"We have to keep fighting," Red Arrow replied grimly. "For justice. For the people of Star City."\n\nSuddenly, Wonder Woman let out a cry of pain and stumbled back. Cheshire had turned on her, striking her in the back with a hidden blade.\n\n"What have you done?" Green Arrow shouted as he rushed to Wonder Woman\'s side.\n\nCheshire grinned. "I just showed her where her loyalties really lie. Now, it\'s just the two of us again."\n\nBut Green Arrow and Red Arrow were not so easily defeated. Together, they launched a furious assault on Cheshire, their arrows finding their mark again and again.\n\nIn the end, it was Cheshire who was left on the ground, defeated and helpless. Wonder Woman, still recovering from her injury, looked on with a mix of horror and awe.\n\n"You two truly are champions of justice," she said finally. "I should never have doubted you."\n\nGreen Arrow smiled. "No hard feelings. It\'s all in a day\'s work."\n\nAnd with that, the three heroes parted ways, ready for whatever new adventure awaited them in the world of the Justice League.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=2000, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: None, lora_request: None, prompt_adapter_request: None.
