e button\nfunction draw() {\n  // Draw roulette\n  context.fillStyle = "white";\n  context.fillRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);\n  context.strokeStyle = "black";\n  context.beginPath();\n  context.arc(canvas.width/2, canvas.height/2, canvas.width/2-10, 0, 2*Math.PI);\n  context.stroke();\n  for (var i = 0; i < participants.length; i++) {\n    var angle = i * (2*Math.PI/participants.length);\n    context.save();\n    context.translate(canvas.width/2, canvas.height/2);\n    context.rotate(angle);\n    context.textAlign = "center";\n    context.fillText(participants[i], 0, -canvas.width/2+30);\n    context.restore();\n  }\n  // Draw button\n  context.fillStyle = "red";\n  context.fillRect(canvas.width/2-30, canvas.height-70, 60, 40);\n  context.fillStyle = "white";\n  context.font = "20px Arial";\n  context.fillText("Rotate", canvas.width/2, canvas.height-40);\n}\n\n// Function to select a random participant and display the result\nfunction spin() {\n  var result = Math.floor(Math.random() * participants.length);\n  document.getElementById("result").innerHTML = "The winner is " + participants[result] + "!";\n}\n\n//Load the participants and draw the spinner and button on page load\nwindow.onload = function() {\n  draw();\n  document.getElementById("canvas").addEventListener("click", spin);\n}\n```\nBriefly, this code loads the participants from a CSV file using the loadCSV() function, which reads the file and adds the participants to an array. Then use the draw() function to draw the spinner\nuser: It is rumored that in March 2023 they will release the GPT-4 version of Bing and ChatGPT.\nWhat improvements could GPT-4 have over GPT-3.5?\nassistant: GPT-4, as a language model, could have significant advances compared to its previous version, GPT-3.5. Some of these advances could include:\n\n* Increase in size and number of parameters, allowing you to learn more skills and knowledge from large data sets.\n\n* Greater ability to understand and generate natural lang