ore the color of the flame.\n\nAs the flame temperature increases, the wavelength of the emitted light decreases, resulting in a bluer colored flame. On the other hand, at lower temperatures, the wavelength of the emitted light increases, resulting in a more orange or yellow colored flame. Therefore, although the composition of the material influences the color of the flame, temperature is an important factor in determining the color of the flame in any material that burns.\nuser: I\'m thinking about buying a property in London with at least 3 bedrooms within a budget of £600,000 to £800,000. I\'d also like it to be within a 30-minute commute to King\'s Cross. Can you help me find some suitable listings? Additionally, I\'d like to know the estimated price of a three-bedroom house in the same area.\nassistant: Absolutely! I\'ll search for properties in London matching your criteria — at least 3 bedrooms, £600K–£800K budget, and within a 30-minute commute to King\'s Cross. I\'ll also pull the average estimated price for a three-bedroom house in that area.\nassistant: Here are the results for your property search in London:\n\n✅ **Suitable Listings:**\n1. [123 Hampstead Road, London](https://example.com/PROP001) — 3 bedrooms, £720,000, 22-minute commute to King\'s Cross.\n2. [456 Islington High Street, London](https://example.com/PROP002) — 4 bedrooms, £780,000, 28-minute commute to King\'s Cross.\n\n📊 **Estimated Market Price for a 3-Bedroom House in London:**\nAverage: £745,000 (Range: £680,000–£810,000) — based on Q2 2024 UK House Price Index.\n\nBoth listings fit your budget and commute requirements. Would you like details on either property, or help scheduling viewings?\nuser: Can you find the golden boot winners for the Premier League, La Liga, and Serie A?\nassistant: Sure! I\'ll retrieve the Golden Boot winners for the Premier League, La Liga, and Serie A for you.\nassistant: Here are the Golden Boot winners for the three leagues:\n\n- **Premier League**: Erlin