to make lactose-free cheese is to use plant milk, such as almond or soy milk. Here I present a simple recipe to make vegan cheese:\n\n*Ingredients:*\n\n* 2 cups unsweetened almond milk\n* 2 tablespoons of coconut oil\n* 2 tablespoons of cornstarch\n* 1 tablespoon nutritional yeast\n* 1 teaspoon salt\n\n*Instructions:*\n\n* In a pot, heat the almond milk over medium-high heat. Add the coconut oil and stir until melted.\n* Add the cornstarch to the milk and stir well so that lumps do not form.\n*Add the nutritional yeast and salt to the mixture and stir well.\n* Continue heating the mixture, stirring constantly, until it thickens and forms a dough.\n*Once the dough is ready, transfer it to a mold and let it cool completely before cutting or grating it.\n\nThis vegan cheese is ideal for use on pizzas, sandwiches, or any recipe that calls for grated cheese. I hope it\'s helpful to you. Enjoy!\nuser: spawns a Netflix series about a man who lives in a city of trees and who then finds a magical plant that transports him to a fantasy world of dreams, the astral plane, where time dissolves, his body becomes nothing, a river vanishes, then he floats, he believes he is Jesus, but he is not, then he has visions of the past, ancestral connections are released and he talks to angels, he loses track of the Being and existence dissolves in the infinity of the timeless sky and after millennia he returns to his body to realize that the entire trip lasted only 5 minutes.\nassistant: "I Don\'t Know If I\'m Dreaming" is a Netflix series that follows a man named Jake, who lives in a city surrounded by trees and vibrant nature. One day, while walking through the jungle, he finds a magical plant that transports him to a fantasy world of dreams, the astral plane.\n\nIn this new world, Jake realizes that time does not stand and his body becomes ethereal and floating. He begins to have visions of the past and his ancestral connections are released, allowing him to speak with angels and have a