s of propositional logic\nassistant: 1. Axiom of Identity: The proposition "P" is deduced from the proposition "P".\n\n2. Axiom of Double Negation: The proposition "No Not P" is deduced from the proposition "P".\n\n3. Axiom of Commutativity: The proposition "P or Q" is deduced from the proposition "Q or P".\n\n4. Axiom of Associativity: The proposition "(P or Q) or R" is deduced from the proposition "P or (Q or R)".\n\n5. Axiom of Addition: The proposition "P or Q" is deduced from the proposition "P" and the proposition "Q".\n\n6. Axiom of Distribution: The proposition "(P and Q) or R" is deduced from the proposition "P or R" and the proposition "Q or R".\n\n7. Axiom of Simplicity: The proposition "P and F" is deduced from the proposition "P".\n\n8. Axiom of Reduction: The proposition "P or F" is deduced from the proposition "P".<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=2000, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: None, lora_request: None, prompt_adapter_request: None.
