turally by the body from other amino acids, and can also be obtained through diet in foods such as meat and dairy products. L-Carnitine plays an important role in fat metabolism, helping the body convert fat into energy.\n\nIn terms of supplementation, L-Carnitine has been promoted as a supplement that can help lose body fat and improve athletic performance. However, the scientific evidence on the effects of L-Carnitine on fat loss is mixed, and more studies are needed to determine whether it is effective or not.\n\nSome studies have found that L-Carnitine can help improve fat loss and athletic performance in certain circumstances, such as when combined with physical exercise and a proper diet. Other studies, however, have not found any significant fat loss benefit from L-Carnitine supplementation.\n\nAs for the dosage, the recommended amount of L-Carnitine varies depending on each person\'s goal and health status. Generally, the recommended daily dose of L-Carnitine is 500 to 2000 mg per day, and it can be taken in the form of capsules, tablets or powder.\n\nIt is important to note that L-Carnitine supplementation may have side effects in some people, such as nausea, diarrhea, and upset stomach. Additionally, if you have any pre-existing health conditions or are taking any medications, it is important to speak with a doctor before taking any L-Carnitine supplement.\n\nIn conclusion, although L-Carnitine may have some potential benefits for fat loss and sports performance, the scientific evidence is inconclusive and more studies are needed. If you decide to take L-Carnitine supplements, it is important to do so with caution and speak to a healthcare professional first. Additionally, it is important to remember that no supplement can replace a balanced diet and a healthy lifestyle.\nuser: Are there L-Carnitine supplements suitable for vegetarians? And vegan?\nassistant: According to the www.bonusan.es website, the Bonusan supplement with L-carnitine is suitable for v