INFO 09-21 18:30:44 logger.py:37] Received request chatcmpl-852a2c0e687f4c459ce13d3ed96298da: prompt: '<|im_start|>system\nYou are building a long-term memory for an AI assistant. From the dialogue excerpt, extract atomic fact memories as a JSON object: {"memories": ["<single declarative sentence>", ...]}. Keep identifiers, addresses, URLs and configuration values VERBATIM. One fact per entry; include the user preference, attribute or event each entry refers to. Output JSON only.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nDialogue excerpt:\nassistant: Chord progressions are a series of chords played in a specific order that form the harmonic foundation of a piece of music. Chords are groups of notes played simultaneously, usually consisting of a root note and other notes from the same scale. Chord progressions create a sense of movement and tension in music, which can be resolved or left unresolved, depending on the desired effect.\n\nA scale, in music theory, is a sequence of notes arranged in ascending or descending order by pitch. Scales are the building blocks of both melodies and chord progressions. There are several types of scales, with the most common ones being the major scale and the minor scale. Each scale has a specific pattern of intervals (the distance between notes) that gives it a unique sound and character.\n\nWhen composing a melody, it\'s essential to know the scale you\'re working in, as it will determine the pool of notes you can use to create your melody. If you\'re also writing a chord progression, the chords will typically be built using the notes from the same scale. By using the notes of the chords in your melody, you can create a sense of harmony and coherence between the melody and the chord progression.\n\nTo get started with writing a melody, you can follow these steps:\n\nChoose a scale: Pick a scale to work with, such as the major or minor scale. The scale will determine the overall mood of your melody (e.g., happy, sad, or tense).\n\nDetermine the key: Select a key for your melody, which will be the starting note (or root) of your scale. The key determines the pitch center of your melody and can be changed to modulate the piece of music to create variation and interest.\n\nCreate a chord progression: Use the notes from your chosen scale to build chords and arrange them in a sequence that sounds pleasing and harmonically interesting. Common progressions include the I-IV-V-I and ii-V-I in major keys, and i-iv-V-i and i-VI-III-VII in minor keys.\n\nWrite your melody: Start experimenting with the notes from your chosen scale and the chords in your progression. Create a series of short phrases or motifs that can be combined, repeated, or varied to form a complete melody. Try to incorporate a mix of stepwise motion (moving between adjacent notes in the scale) and leaps (skipping notes) to create interest and variety.\n\nAdd rhythm: Incorporate rhythmic patterns and variations to give your melody a sense of movement and structure. Use a mix of short and long notes, syncopation, and rests to create a dynamic and engaging melody.\n\nBy following these steps and understanding the relationship between scales, chords, and melodies, you\'ll be well on your way to creating your own original compositions.\nuser: I\'m thinking about adopting a cat, but I don\'t know how to start. I don\'t know if they involve a lot of work, what needs they normally have. It would also be very useful for me to know which of the various cat breeds there are best resistant to heat, since I am in an arid place.\nassistant: I\'m glad you\'re thinking about adopting a cat. Cats are very intelligent, affectionate and fun animals. To adopt a cat, there are a few things you should keep in mind:\n\n- The first thing is to choose an entity that offers cats for adoption, such as a shelter, shelter or association. There they will ask you some questions to find out if you are suitable to take care of a cat and they will show you the available cats. \n- The second thing is to interact with the cats and choose the one you like the most or that suits you. You can look at their personality, their age, their size and their appearance.\n- The third thing is to comply with the legal and health requirements to adopt a cat. Typically you will have to sign an adoption contract, pay a nominal fee, and take the cat to the vet to have it vaccinated, dewormed, and spayed if it is not already.\n- The fourth thing is to prepare your house to receive the new member of the family. You should have a comfortable and safe place for the cat, as well as food, water, sand, toys and scratching posts.\n\nAs for the cat breeds that resist the heat better, there are some that adapt better to hot and dry climates due to their short, fine fur or their geographical origin. Some of these breeds are the Abyssinian, Bengal, Siamese, Oriental, and Sphynx. However, remember that the most important thing is that the cat has access to fresh water and shade at all times.\n\nI hope I have helped you with your decision to adopt a cat. If you have any other questions or concerns about this topic or any other, do not hesitate to contact me. I\'m here to help you with whatever you need. 😊\nuser: OK, thanks a lot. Do you by any chance know what vaccines a small cat should receive?<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=2000, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: None, lora_request: None, prompt_adapter_request: None.
