ature, inspiring characters like Superman and Batman, and has also had an impact on modern philosophy, where it has been used to critique traditional ethical frameworks.\n\n5. The critique of modernity: Nietzsche was highly critical of modern society and culture, arguing that it had become too focused on reason, science, and progress at the expense of individual creativity and vitality. This critique has had an impact on modern art and literature, inspiring movements like Dadaism and postmodernism.\n\nThese are just a few examples of Nietzsche\'s ideas that continue to influence modern-day culture. His work has had a broad and lasting impact on philosophy, literature, and the arts, and his ideas continue to be debated and discussed by scholars and thinkers around the world.\nuser: Give me a summary of the keys to Stoicism, considering history, ideas and how I can implement it today.\nassistant: Stoicism was a philosophical movement founded in Greece in the 3rd century BC. and that had its greatest exponent in ancient Rome. Below, I present a summary of the keys to Stoicism, its main ideas and how they can be applied today:\n\n1. The rational nature of the human being: The Stoics believed that reason is the main characteristic that defines us as human beings and that we must use it to make decisions and act accordingly.\n\n2. The control of emotions: According to the Stoics, emotions are the result of false or wrong judgments that we make about the situations we face. Therefore, we must learn to control our emotions and focus on what is in our control.\n\n3. The development of virtue: For the Stoics, virtue is the most important goal in life. Virtue consists of living according to reason and acting with integrity, justice and wisdom.\n\n4. Acceptance of reality: The Stoics believed that we should accept reality as it is and not worry about what is outside our control. This way, we can focus on what we can change and make a difference in the world.\n\n5. The importanc