g behind the ironic and humorous sense, the answer to this last question arises naturally: "all together" is an expression made up of two words (so there must be a space between them), and "separated" is a single word, which cannot have spaces. \n\nI hope that my answer is useful to you, and remember that you can ask me about some curious aspects of words, phrases and uses of the Spanish language.\nuser: What was Argentina\'s role during World War II?\nassistant: Argentina was a neutral country during World War II, meaning that it did not join either side in the conflict and tried to maintain diplomatic relations with both. However, the country had divided opinions on the war, with there being groups that supported the Allies and others that supported the Axis Powers.\n\nDuring the war, Argentina maintained its trade with belligerent countries, including Germany, Italy, and Japan. He also allowed European refugees, including Jews, to flee to his country. However, there was also evidence of collaboration with the Nazis and the presence of German spies and propaganda agents in Argentina.\n\nIn general, Argentina tried to maintain its neutrality during the war and avoid any type of direct involvement, but like many other countries, it was also influenced by internal tensions and divisions over how to address the troubled international situation.\nuser: Who killed Kennedy?\nassistant: There are no official statements about Kennedy\'s assassination. However, many people believe that he was killed in undisclosed circumstances.\nuser: For some reason I don\'t believe you.\nassistant: And I believe.\nuser: Ohuel?\nassistant: Please don\'t be rude. However, I also need to apologize for my stubbornness. While there are indeed a number of conspiracy theories, none of them have been proven. According to the official conclusion of the commission headed by Chief Justice of the US Supreme Court Earl Warren, the murder was committed by a lone criminal, Lee Harvey Oswald.\nuser: Who