ere:\n\n* A, B and C are the coefficients of the general equation of the line Ax + By + C = 0.\n* x and y are the coordinates of the point.\n* sqrt is the square root function.\n* | | indicates the absolute value.  \n\nTo use this formula, you must know the coordinates of the point and the coefficients of the general equation of the line. These values \u200b\u200bare then substituted into the formula and solved to obtain the distance d.\n\nIt is important to note that if the distance is positive, the point is on the opposite side of the line to which the normal points, while if it is negative it is on the same side.\nuser: But if I don\'t have the general equation of the line? I only know that the line passes through two points: P1 = (x1, y1) and P2 = (x2, y2)\nassistant: If you have the points `P1 = (x1, y1)` and `P2 = (x2, y2)` that the line passes through, you can find the equation of the line in slope-intercept form using the slope formula:\n\n`m = (y2 - y1) / (x2 - x1)`\n\nOnce you have the slope, you can use the point-slope equation of the line to find the equation of the line:\n\n`y - y1 = m(x - x1)`\n\nOnce you have the equation of the line, you can find the distance between a point `P3 = (x3, y3)` and the line using the point-line distance formula:\n\n`d = |(y3 - y1) - m(x3 - x1)| /sqrt(1 + m^2)`\n\nWhere m is the slope of the line and (x1, y1) is one of the points through which the line passes.\n\nNote that there are two possible solutions for the point-line distance, since the line can be above or below the point. To ensure you have the correct distance, you must take the absolute value of the formula result.\nuser: During the first volume of Harry Potter, the three heroes must solve a riddle - which requires no magic - in order to access the room where the philosopher\'s stone is hidden. This problem consists of finding two potions among the seven in front of them: those that allow you to move forward and backward. They are helped by a few clues:\n\n- Th