oncluded with the victory of the Bourbon candidate, and his acceptance by the other European powers with the signing of the Treaty of Utrecht, which, among other things, prevented a dynastic union between Spain and France, dispelling fears. that I previously mentioned. Would you like more information about the War of the Spanish Succession?\nuser: Act as a travel expert and make me an extensive and detailed travel guide for a specific destination. Please write a 1000 word SEO optimized guide with h3, h3 headings, lists and an FAQ section on frequently asked questions of interest from travelers. The destination is [destiny]\nassistant: Japan travel guide\nJapan is a unique and fascinating destination, with a unique combination of tradition and advanced technology. Known for its futuristic cities, ancient temples, vibrant pop culture, and delicious food, Japan is a destination that impresses all travelers. Here I present a complete guide to help you plan your trip to Japan.\n\nHistory and culture\nJapan is an island with a rich history and culture, with Chinese and Korean influences. Japanese tradition is reflected in its architecture, art, clothing and way of daily life. Japanese culture is known for its respect for elders, its work ethic, and its appreciation of nature and beauty.\n\nClimate\nJapan has a temperate climate with distinct seasons. Spring is known for its cherry blossoms, summer is warm and humid, autumn is cool and beautiful with tree leaves changing color, and winter is cold with snowfall in mountainous regions.\n\nHow to get there\nThe closest international airport to Japan is Narita International Airport in Tokyo. There are also other international airports in other cities such as Osaka and Nagoya. From the airport, you can take a train or a bus to the city center.\n\nAccommodation\nThere is a wide variety of accommodation options in Japan, from luxury hotels to budget hostels. Popular options include ryokan, which are traditional Japanese accommodations with tatami mats and futons, and capsule hotels, which are small rooms with beds and televisions.\n\nMeal\nJapanese food is an important part of the country\'s culture. From sushi to ramen, there are many delicious options to try. It is also common to find street food markets throughout the country, where you can try a wide variety of local dishes.\n\nTourist places\nThere are many tourist places you must visit in Japan, including:\nTokyo: The capital of Japan is a vibrant and lively city, with much to offer in terms of history, culture, food and entertainment.\n\nGolden Dragon Temple (Kinkaku-ji) in Kyoto: This three-story temple is famous for its golden façade and beautiful gardens.\n\nMount Fuji: This active volcano is the highest point in Japan and one of the most impressive views in the country.\n\nMeiji Shrine in Tokyo: This shrine dedicated to the Meiji imperial couple is one of the most popular places for tourists in Tokyo.\n\nTokyo Imperial Palace: This palace is the home of Japan\'s imperial family and is a stunning place to visit.\n\nUeno Park in Tokyo: This park is home to a zoo, an art museum, and a Buddhist temple.\n\nTokyo Tower: This observation tower offers panoramic views of the city and is a popular place to watch the sunset.\n\nHiroshima Shrine: This shrine commemorates the victims of the atomic bomb attack on Hiroshima in 1945.\n\nTóquio Temple: This temple is one of the oldest in Japan and is known for its beautiful gardens and impressive architecture.\n\nDotonbori Street in Osaka: This lively street is known for its bright signs and street food restaurants.\nuser: Why is Mount Fuji so important in Japan?\nassistant: Mount Fuji occupies a considerable place in ancient Japanese religion and beliefs. He is often called Fujiyama and Fuji-San (Mr. Fuji) because he is worshiped as a god of Japan, a "kami", a popular deity of the Shinto religion. In fact, due to its volcanic activities, it symbolizes both the earth and sky and fire.\n\nTherefore, many people go there to make a pilgrimage to the top of Mount Fuji either by walking or taking the cable car. From the foot of the mountain to its summit, it is not difficult to find sanctuaries during the excursion, as well as hot springs directly fed by the volcanic activity of Mount Fuji.\n\nDue to its cultural importance and high altitude, it was inscribed in the UNESCO Cultural Heritage under the name "Fujisan, sacred place and source of artistic inspiration."<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=2000, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: None, lora_request: None, prompt_adapter_request: None.
