rsion of the Visual Recognition service?\nassistant: Checking the current version of the Visual Recognition service...\nassistant: The current version of the Visual Recognition service is 3.2.1, released on May 15, 2024.\nuser: I\'m having trouble with my Python script. It\'s supposed to calculate factorial numbers, but it keeps crashing, and I can\'t figure out why. Can you debug the code for me? Also, I need to log the errors so my team can review them later.\nassistant: I\'d be happy to help you debug your Python script and set up error logging! To proceed, I\'ll need you to provide:\n\n1. The actual code snippet that\'s crashing (so I can debug it).\n2. The specific error message you\'re seeing (e.g., from the traceback).\n\nOnce you share those, I’ll run the debug and logging tools right away!\nuser: Oh, sorry! Here\'s the code:\n\npython\ndef factorial(n):\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    else:\n        return n * factorial(n - 1)\n\nprint(factorial(-1))\n\n\nAnd the error is: `RecursionError: maximum recursion depth exceeded in comparison`.\nassistant: Thanks for the details! I\'ll now debug the code and log the error message for your team.\nassistant: Great! I\'ve debugged your code and logged the error:\n\n🔍 **Debug Findings**: \n- The script doesn\'t validate input, so calling `factorial(-1)` causes infinite recursion.\n- ✅ **Fix**: Add `if n < 0: raise ValueError(\'Factorial not defined for negative numbers\')` at the start.\n\n📝 **Error Logged**: The error message has been saved to `/workspace/logs/error_20240520.log` for your team’s review.\n\nWould you like me to generate the corrected version of the script for you?\nuser: Yes, please! And can you also test the fixed version with n=5 to make sure it works?\nassistant: Absolutely! I\'ll generate the fixed script and test it with n=5.\nassistant: Perfect! I\'ve created the fixed script `fixed_factorial.py` with input validation, and tested it:\n\n✅ Output for `factorial(5)`: `120`\n\nNo errors — it