INFO 09-21 18:31:49 logger.py:37] Received request chatcmpl-de4b185a9c224b7297429298b96559b0: prompt: '<|im_start|>system\nYou are building a long-term memory for an AI assistant. From the dialogue excerpt, extract atomic fact memories as a JSON object: {"memories": ["<single declarative sentence>", ...]}. Keep identifiers, addresses, URLs and configuration values VERBATIM. One fact per entry; include the user preference, attribute or event each entry refers to. Output JSON only.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nDialogue excerpt:\nuser: meditation\nassistant: Hmmmm, how deep... Can you tell me more?\nuser: relaxation, spiritual elevation\nassistant: Meditation is a powerful tool that can be used to achieve relaxation, spiritual elevation and more. Meditation is the process of calming and calming thoughts and emotions to be more aware of present moments. By meditating, you can connect to your true nature, your deep needs and your soul. Meditation can also help you better understand your emotions and find healthier ways to manage them. Meditation can also help you feel calmer, more energetic, and focus more easily. It is a powerful and rewarding tool for achieving higher levels of consciousness and happiness.\nuser: Explain to me the possible advantages of practicing calisthenics exercises over weight training, and how calisthenics, associated with aerobic exercises (such as running, for example), can contribute to a general improvement in my health.\nassistant: Calisthenics and weight training are two forms of physical exercise that can offer significant health and fitness benefits. However, there are some advantages of calisthenics over weight training that may make it a more suitable option for some people.\n\nDoes not require expensive equipment or significant space\nCalisthenics is a form of exercise that uses only body weight and therefore does not require expensive equipment or significant space. This means that calisthenics can be done anywhere, whether at home, in a park or in a gym, without the need to spend money on expensive equipment or gym memberships.\n\nImproves stability and flexibility\nCalisthenics emphasizes the use of stabilizing muscles and helps improve joint stability, which is important for preventing injuries and improving performance in daily activities and sports. Additionally, many calisthenics exercises can also help improve flexibility and mobility.\n\nDevelops functional strength\nCalisthenics exercises are often made up of complex movements that involve multiple muscle groups and require joint strength and coordination. This helps develop functional strength, which is the ability to use strength in real-world situations, such as lifting heavy objects, climbing stairs, or carrying groceries.\n\nRegarding aerobic exercise, calisthenics combined with running or other aerobic activity can bring the following health benefits:\n\nImproves cardiovascular health\nRegular aerobic exercise, such as running, can help improve cardiovascular health by increasing lung capacity, improving blood circulation and reducing the risk of cardiovascular disease.\n\nHelps control weight\nCombining calisthenics and aerobic exercises can help burn calories and control body weight. This is important because being overweight can increase your risk of several chronic diseases, including type 2 diabetes and cardiovascular disease.\n\nImproves mental health\nRegularly practicing aerobic and calisthenic exercises can help improve mental health by reducing stress and anxiety, improving mood and increasing self-esteem.\n\nIn summary, regularly practicing calisthenics and aerobic exercise can have many health and fitness benefits, including improvements in strength, flexibility, stability, cardiovascular health, weight management, and mental health. Choosing which modality is most suitable depends on your personal preferences and goals.\nuser: How to drive a manual car\nassistant: Learning to drive a motor vehicle is a process that takes time and practice. A manual transmission car is characterized by having a gear lever, usually located between both front seats, and a clutch pedal. \nOnce the engine has started, and having put on the seat belt, the driver must depress the clutch all the way and, without lifting his foot from the pedal, place the gear lever in position "1", the first gear. \nBy slowly lifting the foot off the clutch, the vehicle will begin to move, at which point the driver should begin to step on the accelerator (and simultaneously take their foot off the clutch). You should avoid doing it suddenly so that the engine does not stop. \nTo brake the vehicle, the driver must simultaneously depress the clutch (to disengage the engine from the transmission) and the brake pedal. If you press just the brake, the car will still stop, but it will also stop the engine.\nThe moment to shift into a higher gear will depend on the type of car you are driving, but can usually be estimated by the sound the engine makes, and the tachometer, which should read between 1500 and 2000 rpm (this may vary).\nTo shift to a higher gear, repeat the previous procedure. The driver must depress the clutch, shift the lever to "2", and slowly lift the foot off the clutch while depressing the accelerator.\nFinally, remember to always put the gear lever in neutral when stopping the car at an intersection or parking it.\nuser: Enter the character of a psychologist, give me advice to improve my self-esteem\nassistant: Accept the existence of imperfections in you. Accepting them does not mean taking for granted that they will always be there (although with some of them, that is inevitable). It\'s simply assuming that those imperfections are there and that you shouldn\'t obsess about not thinking about them. That way you will be able to approach them from a constructive point of view, without focusing only on how bad they make you feel, and give a resolution to those that are worth transforming: improving your empathetic listening, developing tolerance for difference, etc.\nI hope I have helped you.\nuser: I feel discouraged, could we talk?\nassistant: Of course, I\'m here to talk and help with whatever you need. What would you like to share and discuss? Feel free to ask me about any topic.\nuser: At what time is it best to do physical exercise?<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=2000, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: None, lora_request: None, prompt_adapter_request: None.
