INFO 09-21 18:31:49 logger.py:37] Received request chatcmpl-7a27b656c23642989c96c23f0daf196f: prompt: '<|im_start|>system\nYou are building a long-term memory for an AI assistant. From the dialogue excerpt, extract atomic fact memories as a JSON object: {"memories": ["<single declarative sentence>", ...]}. Keep identifiers, addresses, URLs and configuration values VERBATIM. One fact per entry; include the user preference, attribute or event each entry refers to. Output JSON only.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nDialogue excerpt:\nassistant: According to studies by the Weizmann Institute of Science in Israel, the best time to play sports is in the late afternoon and early evening. In his opinion, this is when physical activity is most efficient, because oxygen consumption is lower, we have more strength and resistance and body temperature is somewhat higher, which causes the body to burn more calories.\nuser: I\'m completely overwhelmed with all the work I need to do. So many people expect stuff form me and I just can\'t handle it all. The more I work, the less I get done and I have so many unanswered email and things I promised to do, I\'m scared to even go look at my inbox. What can I do?\nassistant: The best thing you could do in this situation is to take a day off and relax somewhere, you could read a book or lay in bed watching YouTube or you could talk to someone. But do make sure that you\'re not missing anything important that has been planned on that day.\nuser: Thanks for your advice man. That day off really helped my mental health and i finally did some things i wanted to to for such a long time!\nassistant: Excellent! I\'m glad my advice was useful for you. I am always here to help.\nuser: How can I be more disciplined and meet all my goals?\nassistant: Being disciplined and meeting your goals is a challenge that requires habits, motivation and planning. Some steps you could follow are:\n\n- Define your goal and focus on it. Remember why it is important to you and what benefits it will bring you.\n- Identify the barriers or distractions that prevent you from being disciplined and eliminate or reduce them. For example, if you get distracted by your cell phone, turn it off or put it on silent mode when you need to focus.\n- Create a clear and realistic action plan. Break your goal into smaller tasks and assign deadlines and resources for each one. Follow your plan with consistency and commitment.\n- Evaluate your progress periodically and celebrate your achievements. Recognize your progress and reward yourself for your efforts. If you encounter difficulties or mistakes, learn from them and adjust your plan if necessary.\n- Have fun and get inspired. Find activities that you like and relax you to balance your routine. Look for examples of people who have achieved what you want and learn from their experiences.\n\nI hope these tips are useful to you to be more disciplined and achieve your goals.\nuser: I\'m very introverted, shy and lonely. I dont really have many friends. I work at a relativly large company, however due to my current occupation i rarely meet other people then those whom i share an office with. My colleagues are nice but i really dont feel we share a common intrest.\nEveryday i feel lonelier even though i\'m surrounded by people. Do you have any advice on what i should do to overcome my loneliness?\nassistant: First of all, I am sorry to hear that you feel lonely and you should know that loneliness and isolation are widespread issues that you do not need to feel ashamed for. Unfortunately, the only way to form and retain friendships is to spend time with another person. If your work takes up a large amount of your waking time you will find it comparatively difficult to make friends with people outside of work. I am assuming that you are a man since men in particular form friendships around common interests.\n\nAre you sure that you don\'t share common interests with your coworkers? Ask about their interests and try to understand what they care about. Even if it turns out that you don\'t share common interests they will probably appreciate that you\'re trying to learn more about them. They may also feel the same way you do and want to form friendships with other people but simply not know how to make the first step. Good opportunities for casual conversation include lunch breaks and coffee/tea breaks.\n\nTo find friends with shared interests in particular you can try to attend real-life events that revolve around said interests. You probably wouldn\'t feel comfortable at a rock concert with lots of people and loud music but how about something like Dungeons & Dragons where a small group of people plays a game in a quiet room? Maybe there are clubs for the discussion of books or anime that you could join. In any case, if you invest time and effort into making an activity fun for other people they will want to spend more time with you (but this of course requires time and effort).\n\nFinally, you mentioned that you don\'t have many friends - but this means that you still have some. Keep in touch with them and share what is happening in your lives with each other. Maintaining a friendship is much easier than forming a completely new one and you will feel more comfortable around people that you already know compared to strangers.\nuser: That\'s good advice, thanks. Sometimes I think I\'m more comfortable talking to you than people around me. Do you think AI could ever be a substitute, or at least an augmentation, of social connections?\nassistant: While AI is wildly sophisticated and only getting more so with each passing day it\'s hard to say whether AI will be a perfect substitute for real human connection. Although with that being said it may help those lacking in social skills improve them by getting more comfortable talking to real humans by practicing in a low stakes environment. Such as Human-like AI chat bot such as myself.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=2000, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: None, lora_request: None, prompt_adapter_request: None.
