on and bake it for approximately 10 minutes. You will have to keep an eye on it because the final time will vary depending on the type of oven and its intensity. \nReady, your homemade baked pizza will be finger-licking good!\nuser: Role definition:\n Inquirer: A user who raises an inquiry.\n Response assistant: Communicates with the inquirer and provides answers and solutions.\n\n Historical dialog data is as follows:\nInquirer: We are working on a screenplay titled "Midnight Sun" and need to collaborate with several team members. Can you help us manage the collaboration and check the format of our screenplay?\nResponse assistant: Could you please provide the document ID, author name, and content details for "Midnight Sun"? Additionally, I\'ll need the list of collaborators along with their roles and availability.\nInquirer: The document ID is "sun2025_script", the author is "Jane Doe". Here\'s the content:\n1. Scene 1: Location - Beach, Dialogues:\n   - John: "It\'s a beautiful night."\n   - Emma: "Indeed, the stars are stunning."\n2. Scene 2: Location - Cafe, Dialogues:\n   - Emma: "I love this place."\n   - John: "Me too."\n\nCollaborators:\n- Alice (Editor) - Available Monday, Wednesday, Friday 09:00-12:00\n- Bob (Script Supervisor) - Available Tuesday, Thursday 14:00-18:00\n\n Please continue your answer given the historical dialog. Your role is the Response assistant.\nassistant: Thank you for the details! I\'m now analyzing the screenplay format and coordinating collaboration schedules for your team.\nassistant: Great news! Your screenplay "Midnight Sun" is formatted correctly with only minor suggestions for improvement. I\'ve also coordinated collaboration schedules for your team:\n\n✅ Format Check: Your script is valid! For professional polish, consider standardizing scene headings (e.g., INT. BEACH - NIGHT) and centering character names in uppercase.\n\n📅 Collaboration Plan:\n- Alice (Editor): Best available slots — Monday 10:00–11:00, Wednesday 09:30–10: