nd accessible public transportation: This could include implementing a fast, frequent and affordable public transportation system that connects all areas of the city. In addition, sustainable means of transportation such as bicycles, electric scooters and walking can be promoted.\n\nIntegrate green spaces into the urban fabric: Green spaces provide multiple benefits for health and well-being, as well as for the environment. The inclusion of green areas in urban planning could include the creation of parks and gardens in urban areas, the integration of green spaces in buildings, the installation of green roofs and the creation of green zones in recreation areas.\n\nPromote affordable housing: One of the biggest concerns of people in urban areas is the cost of housing. One solution could be the implementation of public policies that encourage the construction of affordable housing in urban areas and the protection of already existing affordable housing.\n\nPromote citizen participation in urban planning: Citizen participation can help ensure that urban planning is fair and representative of community needs. This could include creating citizen committees that take an active role in urban planning and gathering citizen feedback and input into the planning process.\n\nAddress urban exclusion and promote social inclusion: Urban areas can be centers of exclusion and marginalization. It is important to address these issues and promote social inclusion in urban development planning. This could include creating programs and services that help vulnerable people, creating local employment, improving education and health services, and removing architectural and social barriers that prevent people from participating in urban life.\n\nIn summary, equitable and sustainable urban planning requires an integrated approach and active community participation. It is important to consider the needs and concerns of the community at all times and work to create a city that is livable for all its inhabitants.\nuser: Explains quantum computing in a simple way.\nassistant: Quantum computer science is a field of computer science that is based on quantum physics for calculations. Instead of using bits, as in classical computer science, quantum computer science uses qubits, which can be in several states at the same time.\n\nThis means that quantum computer science has the ability to calculate much faster than classic computer science, especially for complex problems such as cryptography, molecular simulation and automatic learning. Quantum computer science also has the potential to solve problems that are too complex for classical computer science.\n\nAlthough quantum computer science is emerging technology, some prototypes have already been developed and researchers continue to work to develop new applications and algorithms to take advantage of their potential. Quantum computer science is considered to have a significant impact on technology and science in the future.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=2000, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: None, lora_request: None, prompt_adapter_request: None.
