ing held down in tkinter.\nuser: How can I setup Gradle sub project?\nassistant: To set up a Gradle subproject, you can follow the steps below:\n\n1. Create a parent project directory and a subproject directory within it.\n\n2. In the parent project directory, create a settings.gradle file and add the following line of code to include the subproject directory:\n\n   ```\n   include \'subproject\'\n   ```\n\n3. In the subproject directory, create a build.gradle file and add the necessary configurations for the subproject.\n\n4. In the parent project directory, create a build.gradle file and add the following code to include the subproject as a dependency:\n\n   ```\n   dependencies {\n       implementation project(\':subproject\')\n   }\n   ```\n\n5. Run the Gradle build command in the parent project directory to build the subproject and its dependencies.\n\n6. You can now use the subproject in your parent project.\n\nThese steps should help you set up a Gradle subproject. Remember to adjust the directory names and configurations to fit your specific project needs.\nI’ll use an ai assistant because I don’t know the topic\nuser: Thank you\nassistant: You are welcome. If you have any more questions please let me know.\nuser: I need to prepare for a parent-teacher conference tomorrow and I need to check the latest messages from my son, his student ID is STUD123. I also need to look up some key dates related to him on the church app, his contact ID is 9875. Plus, I need to convert page 2 of the PDF document named "diploma.pdf" from a folder named "files" to BMP image. Can you help with all that?\nassistant: Of course! I\'ll retrieve your son\'s latest messages, pull the key dates from the church app, and convert page 2 of diploma.pdf to a BMP image — all in one go.\nuser: Thank you! Can you summarize the messages and dates for me so I can print them out for the conference? Also, could you email the BMP image to my wife’s email: wife@example.com?\nassistant: Absolutely! I