art by finding nearby activities around your hotel in Mexico City. I\'ll also look up flight options from MEX to Toronto, explore top destinations in North America for future trips, and retrieve details about your hotel (ID: 7744) including transport links. Let me gather all that for you.\nassistant: Now I\'ll check the hotel details for ID 7744, including nearby transport options and amenities.\nassistant: Next, I\'ll look up the best airlines operating flights from Mexico City (MEX) to Toronto (YYZ) next month.\nassistant: Finally, I\'ll identify some top cities and destinations in North America worth considering for your future travel plans.\nassistant: Here\'s your complete travel plan summary:\n\n1. **Nearby Activities Near Your Hotel (ID: 2341)**:\n   - Chapultepec Park (1.2 km, 4.8★)\n   - National Museum of Anthropology (2.5 km, 4.9★)\n   - Coyoacán Historic Center (4.1 km, 4.7★)\n\n2. **Hotel Details (Hotel Casa de la Sierra, ID: 7744)**:\n   - Address: Paseo de la Reforma 123, Juárez, Mexico City\n   - Transport Links: Metro Line 3 (Juárez Station, 0.3 km), Metrobús Line 1 (0.5 km)\n   - Amenities: Free WiFi, breakfast, 24-hour front desk, airport shuttle\n\n3. **Best Flights from MEX to YYZ (Next Month)**:\n   - Air Canada: $580, direct, 4.6★\n   - Aeromexico: $520, direct, 4.5★ (Best Value)\n   - Lufthansa: $710, connecting, 4.3★\n\n4. **Top North American Destinations for Future Trips**:\n   - Banff, Canada: Stunning mountain landscapes\n   - New Orleans, USA: Vibrant jazz and Creole cuisine\n   - Vancouver, Canada: Urban life meets coastal beauty\n   - Oaxaca, Mexico: Rich cultural traditions\n   - Quebec City, Canada: Historic European charm\n\nLet me know if you\'d like help booking flights or reserving tickets to any of these attractions!\nuser: Can you place an order at Starbucks for me? I\'d like a Grande Cappuccino and two Blueberry Muffins.\nassistant: Of course! I\'ll place your order for a Grande Cappuccino and two Blueberry Muffins at Starbuc